-# Integrated bridge management prototype
-
-The manager now runs inside Hookshot's backend, room widget and text commands. The former standalone fixture manager has been removed. Product code lives in `src/bridgeManagement`, `src/BridgeManagementRuntime.ts`, `src/config/sections/BridgeManagement.ts`, and `web/components/roomConfig/BridgeManagementConfig.tsx`.
-
-## Architecture
-
-| Layer                      | Responsibility                                                                                                                                               |
-| -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
-| Hookshot widget            | Existing Preact UI and Matrix OpenID session; room-first cross-network discovery, destination selection, matching suggestions, mappings and relay Matrix IDs |
-| Hookshot runtime           | Existing service permissions, live Matrix room membership/power checks, account delegation and allowed rooms                                                 |
-| TypeScript coordinator     | Validated versioned contracts, serialized operations, expected-room checks and SQLite operation journal                                                      |
-| Bridge management endpoint | Authenticated in-process access to bridge account/portal databases, caches and network client                                                                |
-| mautrix bridgev2 changes   | Portal-lock-protected mapping operations that preserve shared rooms                                                                                          |
-| LINE extension             | Actual joined-group discovery, database mappings, safe portal actions and relay owner/login resolution                                                       |
-
-A Matrix user ID identifies the relay owner. A bridge login ID selects that owner's remote account. Managers select administrator-approved accounts; remote credentials remain in the bridge. Source and target Matrix permissions are checked for moves, and only this bridge's mapping is modified.
-
-See [configuration and commands](../docs/setup/bridge-management.md) and [source review](BRIDGE_REVIEW.md).
-
-## Build
-
-Use Node 24+, Rust and Go 1.26+. The source bundle contains sibling `hookshot`, `line` and `mautrix-go` directories. LINE's `go.mod` replaces mautrix-go with that sibling checkout containing the shared-room fixes.
-
-From `hookshot`:
-
-```sh
-pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
-pnpm run build:app:rs
-pnpm run build:app
-pnpm run build:web
-pnpm exec vitest --config vitest.unit.config.ts run tests/bridgeManagement
-python3 -m venv .venv-synapse
-.venv-synapse/bin/pip install matrix-synapse==1.162.0
-```
-
-From `line`, build using the framework's supported pure-Go Olm implementation:
-
-```sh
-GOGC=20 GOMEMLIMIT=2GiB GOMAXPROCS=2 go build -p 1 -tags goolm -gcflags='github.com/highesttt/matrix-line-messenger/pkg/ltsm=-N -l' -o matrix-line ./cmd/matrix-line
-```
-
-The generated LINE crypto package is expensive to compile; limiting compiler concurrency and disabling optimization for that generated package avoids excessive build memory. The `goolm` flag selects the framework's Go Olm implementation and does not disable LINE encryption.
-
-## Real stack validation
-
-The native harnesses use real Synapse and actual bridge processes. Each owns its child processes and isolated database directory. Credentials and databases remain ignored; reports and screenshots contain no access tokens.
-
-- `stack/run.py`: Matrix delivery and room isolation.
-- `stack/hookshot-smoke.py`: actual Hookshot joins and bot command responses.
-- `transports/run.py run`: actual WhatsApp and Signal bot/provisioning checks.
-- `transports/run.py run --line-binary /absolute/path/line/matrix-line`: adds the actual LINE bridge in the same rooms.
-- `integrated/run.py`: actual Hookshot OpenID API and compiled widget against the LINE management extension; see its README for runtime paths.
-
-Run Python harnesses with the Synapse virtual environment. Cloud command sessions isolate localhost services, so each combined harness starts services and performs requests in the same execution. They are not public website deployments.
-
-## Scope
-
-The actual bridge-management contract is implemented for the accompanying LINE source. Stock WhatsApp and Signal provisioning does not implement it; their real appservice tests do not pretend otherwise. The shared TypeScript coordinator and framework mapping code are reusable for their management adapters.
-
-Without authenticated external accounts, validation can prove startup, Matrix bot operation, database behavior, access control and logged-out handling, but cannot prove live LINE/WhatsApp/Signal message forwarding. An absent remote login is displayed as **Login required**, separately from an offline bridge or missing capability.
