-# Integrated validation
-
-`run.py` starts an isolated real Synapse, the compiled Hookshot appservice, and the compiled LINE bridge extension. It creates two Matrix rooms, obtains real Matrix OpenID credentials, exchanges them for Hookshot widget sessions, checks account authorization, and renders the compiled Preact widget in Chromium.
-
-The browser parent supplies the Matrix widget messaging handshake and a real Synapse OpenID token. Bridge account data comes from the running LINE management API. No remote LINE account is logged in, so the expected state is **Login required**; the test verifies that chat listing and connect operations cannot fabricate success.
-
-Run after building Hookshot and LINE:
-
-```sh
-npm install --prefix prototypes/integrated
-node prototypes/integrated/node_modules/playwright/cli.js install chromium --only-shell
-python prototypes/integrated/run.py
-```
-
-The harness expects the LINE executable at `../line/matrix-line`, Node on PATH, Python with Synapse and PyYAML installed, and the pinned local Playwright dependency. It binds localhost ports 18008, 19993, 19994, and 29338, refuses occupied ports, uses temporary databases, and terminates only its own processes. Generated evidence is `test-report.json` and `preview.png`. Runtime credentials are temporary and never included in the screenshot or report.
-
-## Illustrative UI walkthrough
-
-After building the widget, run `npm run demo --prefix prototypes/integrated`. This drives the actual compiled widget through browser-intercepted sample API responses for WhatsApp, Signal, and LINE, including destination selection, connecting, moving an existing portal, and selecting its relay account. Every screenshot has an **ILLUSTRATIVE DEMO** banner. These screenshots demonstrate the interface and do not constitute external-network transport tests. Results are recorded separately in `demo-test-report.json`.
